      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-11T04:07:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suggest reading the BMC chip variant via `SOC_FAMILY` in `./meta-phosphor/recipes-graphics/obmc-ikvm/obmc-ikvm_git.bb`.\n\nSOC_FAMILY is already defined in machine includes for supported platforms:\n\n`./meta-aspeed/conf/machine/include/ast2400.inc:1:SOC_FAMILY \u003d \"aspeed-g4\"`\n`./meta-aspeed/conf/machine/include/ast2500.inc:1:SOC_FAMILY \u003d \"aspeed-g5\"`\n`./meta-aspeed/conf/machine/include/ast2600.inc:1:SOC_FAMILY \u003d \"aspeed-g6\"`\n`./meta-aspeed/conf/machine/include/ast2700.inc:1:SOC_FAMILY \u003d \"aspeed-g7\"`\n`./meta-hpe/meta-gxp/conf/machine/include/gxp.inc:11:SOC_FAMILY \u003d \"gxp-b1\"`\n`./meta-nuvoton/conf/machine/include/npcm7xx.inc:29:SOC_FAMILY \u003d \"npcm7xx\"`\n`./meta-nuvoton/conf/machine/include/npcm8xx.inc:32:SOC_FAMILY \u003d \"npcm8xx\"`\n\n\nThen maintain a mapping table in `obmc-ikvm/meson.build` to associate each SOC_FAMILY with its corresponding USB virtual hub platform device entry. With this mapping, developers no longer need to manually check hardware documentation for the base address.\n\n`chip_vhub_map \u003d {`\n`    \u0027aspeed-g4\u0027: \u00271e6a0000.usb-vhub\u0027,`\n`    \u0027aspeed-g5\u0027: \u00271e6a0000.usb-vhub\u0027,`\n`    \u0027aspeed-g6\u0027: \u00271e6a0000.usb-vhub\u0027,`\n`    \u0027aspeed-g7\u0027: \u002712060000.usb-vhub\u0027,`\n`    \u0027npcm7xx\u0027: \u0027f0800000.usb-vhub\u0027,`\n`    \u0027npcm8xx\u0027: \u002710800000.usb-vhub\u0027,`\n`    \u0027gxp-b1\u0027: \u002710040000.usb-vhub\u0027, `\n`}`\n\n@jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com, @hariharanr@ami.com, @eajames@linux.ibm.com, @tomaszx.sankowski@intel.com, @bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com, @ed@tanous.net, @geissonator@yahoo.com, @patrick@stwcx.xyz what do you think?",
      "revId": "11545f25974a67dea71629ce26b38800a7d53eb9",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
