      "writtenOn": "2026-11-16T03:07:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agree that nobody should have to look up the hub address per platform, but I\u0027d solve it at runtime rather than through SOC_FAMILY. Mapping SOC_FAMILY in meson.build ties the build to Yocto\u0027s naming, still needs an obmc-ikvm change for every new SoC, and adds a third copy of what create_usbhid.sh already works out from the DT compatible.\n\nThe daemon can find the hub without any table by enumerating /sys/bus/platform/drivers/aspeed_vhub/. Failing that, matching the DT compatible at runtime the way create_usbhid.sh does keeps it in one place.\n\nAlso, the npcm7xx/npcm8xx entries wouldn\u0027t work as listed. Nuvoton uses ci_hdrc (create_usbhid.sh uses ci_hdrc.0), and the port walk in Input::connect() only fits the aspeed vhub layout.",
      "parentUuid": "85328dd2_4e219ce0",
      "revId": "11545f25974a67dea71629ce26b38800a7d53eb9",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
